Z||000003||DecadenceR||07-24-2001||11:11 AM||||Health Care<BR>Food service<BR>Ummm...<BR>That's all I can think og off the top of the head.||||reg||1
Z||000004||LarryB||07-24-2001||12:08 PM||||It depends on what you mean by "safe".   I look at the term to reflect how easy it would be to get another good job quickly; if your employer goes belly-up nobody's job is safe.<P>Based on that a first-rate Solaris systems administrator (not a pretender) or a CCIE (Cisco Certified Internetworking Expert) are good bets, there aren't enough of them to go around and they're needed by companies in virtually every sector from network providers to engineering firms to the financial services industry.  <P>The most important things are to be very good in your field and to keep up to date with your training so that even if your current employer no longer needs you, someone else will. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ken Wittlief||07-24-2001||01:49 PM||||this is one of the aspects of Future Shock.<P> things in our society change so fast that an entire industry can be on top of the world one day, and in the toilet a year later.<P>  the only thing that seems certain today is change (a good reason to be an engineer - they are people that take stuff and change it to make it better - usually)<P>  if you can somehow capitolize on the fact that things are always changing - you would have a stable career for a while.<P>  But i think in general, no field or career is safe from possible extinction. You could become an undertaker and some smart a$$ will find a way to allow us all to live forever.||||reg||10
Z||000006||Mach10||07-24-2001||02:27 PM||||"Entrepreneur"<BR>Most stable job I can think of!<P><BR>"At least he got a job, he's not a dumb putz,"<BR>"He works for himself, scratchin' his nutz! HA!"<P>-Insane Clown Posse, "What is a Juggolo?"||||reg||7
Z||000007||rogergarrison||07-24-2001||03:12 PM||||doctors, auto body rep, prostitution   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>oh yea if you dont want to do  anything, owning a junkyard or cemetary would be great.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||frontal lobe||07-24-2001||03:26 PM||||Well, being a doctor is pretty recession proof, I must say.  People are living longer, and require more care as they do (hey, old cars need more maintenance, so do people).<P>Also, being a nurse is very safe.  As people age, there is A LOT of need for them.<P>Lots of other healthcare jobs are "safe".<BR>Seems like they are always begging for pharmacists, too, but RossT would know that better than I.<P>BTW, if you are willing to go through the upfront "pain" of schooling to get one of the above jobs, the pay is PRETTY good.||||reg||1
Z||000009||JSocha||07-24-2001||03:43 PM||||DDT = "Donut Distribution Technician".<P>Always have food; cops are always there to protect and "be" served; and what could they really fire you for...putting the wrong glaze on the wrong style of donut's?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000010||Ken Wittlief||07-24-2001||05:49 PM||||I read once that dentists commit suicide more often than people in any other occupation.<P> and single people commit suicide more than married people<P> and by nations, sweden has the highest suicide rate.<P>  so an unmarried dentist in Sweden has about a 0% survival rate.||||reg||1
Z||000011||EdsB52||07-24-2001||06:36 PM||||A homeless guy would be a good occupation. No one is trying to unseat you and take over, you pay no taxes, and you get free meals. Actually, when the economy is bad you get more help as social programs tend to be a little more liberal at those times. Besides, a position is always open and has few willing candidates competing for your position. You don't need a resume, just a stolen shoping cart and some old blankets.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||07-24-2001||06:54 PM||||Retail/convenience store/gas station.  No matter how bad the economy is, everyone still needs gas, smokes, pop, milk, etc.  The hours & pay suck, but I seriously doubt I'll ever get laid off (too bad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">).<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000013||kslish||07-24-2001||07:35 PM||||Education is pretty stable.  Unless people stop having kids, teachers will always be in need.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>You can't become rich being a teacher, but you won't be hurting either in most parts of the country.  And the vacation plan just rocks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>This is all coming from an unemployed science teacher because I spent the past three years in the wireless communication tech field thinking that was were the $$$ would be.  It wasn't too bad until I got let go due to a merger consolidation in May.  It was time for a change anyways.  I got out at just the right time, Arch Wireless is now trading under 10 cents a share....god I'm glad I didn't take any stock options as part of my severence package hehe.<P>Ken S.||||reg||1
Z||000014||AkursedX||07-24-2001||07:45 PM||||I think Law Enforcement is a pretty stable job.  I'm a Criminal Justice major, and the Criminal Justice job fair at our school is freaking enormous!!  <P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||beer_stud_21||07-24-2001||07:52 PM||||ROTFLMFAO @ roger.  <P>Stable jobs:  Hooker- Lots o horny bastards out there.  Just not for me tho.  lol<P>Military-Thats part of the reason its there in the first place.  To give young guys a purpose in life, give them some kills, and some money in their pockets.  Since baby bush somehow got elected I dont think anyone is going to get laid off from the military and time soon.<P>Drug Dealer-  Pays really well, dont really have to pay taxes.  And either way, you dont have to worry about social security being there for you when you get old and grey.  You'll be taken care of one way or another.  <P>-Marlin||||reg||1
